// The canonical Homestuck-flavored shape: a concept is imported, killed
// (so the inverted loop fires), and an EXECUTE clause sits at the tail.
// EXECUTE(NULL) is currently a syntactic no-op (SPEC §4.4.4).

import dead universe U;
U.DIE();
~ATH(!U) {
    print the universe has ended.;
    BIFURCATE [NULL, NULL] U;
} EXECUTE(NULL);
print and yet, the program continues.;
THIS.DIE();
